  "description": "*\"You're going to fall to your death?\"\n\"Huh?\"\n\"I'd prefer you to live if possible. Because if you die, I'll die too.\"*\n\nSeo Hae-Won met a man on a bridge while drunk. He thought they'd accidentally spent a night together, but he told him he'd known Ji-Hun for a very long time. And that's all? At the edge of a cliff in his life, which had seemed so bleak, he nonchalantly reached out.\n\n *\"What I want isn't your gratitude, Ji-Hun.\"\n\"So... are you saying we should date?\"\n\"Dating won't do. That won't satisfy me. Love me. Just like I love you, Ji-Hun.\"*\n\nHae-Won, seemingly stunned by the passionate confession of love from a stranger, simply added refreshingly.\n\n *\"Shall we break it down into five stages?\"\n\"... Stages?\"\n\"Stage one is sex, stage two is kissing.\"*\n\nHe'd already had sex and kissed. So what are the remaining stages three, four, and five? And, who on earth is that man in Seo Hae-Won?\n\n(Source: Ridibooks, translated)",
